<!--
    What the bike drawn says (SPEC §7.9, second page).

    The three offers, in the order the page names them: a plain bike, a bike
    bearing a bolt, a bike bearing a bolt and a cog. They are the very discs
    the map draws for a journey's stations — marker_journey_station and its two
    variants — at the size this page has room for, so the reader meets the
    drawing here and recognises it there rather than learning a symbol twice.

    This is the one page that shows the three side by side, and it is why the
    marks take the bike's two flanks rather than stack in one corner: all three
    bikes are then drawn at the same scale, and the reader compares three
    identical bikes and sees only the marks that differ.

    No text: a drawable carries none (SPEC §9), and the paragraph above it says
    which is which. Decorative for a screen reader, which reads that paragraph.
-->
